{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Solution Set of an Inequality.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Solution Set of an Inequality.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"solution set of an inequality solution set of an inequality","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Solution Set of an Inequality.md","fileName":"Solution Set of an Inequality.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Solution Set of an Inequality","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Linear Inequalities and Intervals]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Linear Inequalities and Intervals","Interval","Graphing Linear Inequalities","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Solution Set of an Inequality.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Solution Set of an Inequality.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"solution set of an inequality solution set of an inequality","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Solution Set of an Inequality.md","fileName":"Solution Set of an Inequality.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Solution Set of an Inequality","heading":"Solution Set of an Inequality","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The solution set of an inequality is the collection of all values that make the comparison true. For (x<3), every real number less than three belongs to the solution set, while three itself does not.\n\nThe set can be represented verbally, with an [[Interval]], or by [[Graphing Linear Inequalities]] on a number line. Boundary inclusion follows the symbol: (<) and (>) exclude an endpoint, while (\\leq) and (\\geq) include it. Substitution of a test value can verify the direction and detect sign mistakes.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Linear Inequalities and Intervals","Interval","Graphing Linear Inequalities","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"p